# Files the Vercel CLI must never upload.
#
# This is separate from .gitignore on purpose: `vercel deploy` reads
# .vercelignore, so a rule that exists only in .gitignore would not protect a
# CLI upload. Keep the two in sync for anything sensitive.

# Customer enquiries — names, companies, emails, phone numbers.
/var/

# Local archives: a zip of this working tree contains both a full copy of .git
# and whatever is in var/, and at ~200MB it would stall the upload anyway.
*.zip

# Build output and dependencies are produced on Vercel, never uploaded.
/.next/
/node_modules/
/out/
/build/

# Local editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
